   "Executed success/failure fixtures and artifact paths at public command boundary T1 acceptance: actual command execution records and artifact paths/manifest hashes retain declared grants/denials. Reject ungranted effects, silent unsafe/AI/network/shell/secrets/publish operations, hidden network, output-directory escape without grant and missing release artifact verification. Foundation requirement gravity/hosted-hello-execution: Compile the D2 hosted hello source through actual Reader, Syntax, macro expansion and hosted execution, preserving stage/source identities and recording the declared stdout effect and granted authority with the produced output. Refusals: Reject malformed source and the same program without stdout authority; a static hello manifest, host-language print or supplied output string cannot establish execution. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence. Release extension release/public-check-command: Through the public gravity executable, check declared hello, core and nontrivial applications for both .qst and .gravity. Retain expected check results/artifacts, exact source path/extension, executable/compiler identity and normalized command stdout/stderr. Internal calls or relabelled extensions are not public command evidence. Reject missing parity with P18T04001 and invalid inputs with owning